# Apple notebook – Practice section

When adding or editing content in `apple.ipynb`:

- **Place new content under Practice**: Add new cells **after** the markdown cell that contains `### **Practice**` and **before** any later `## **Round …**` section (or at the end of the notebook if there is no such section).
- **Heading levels under Practice**:
  - New main topics (e.g. a new problem or concept): use `#### **Topic Name**`.
  - Sub-topics under a main topic (e.g. “Token Bucket” under “Rate Limiter”): use `##### **Sub-topic**`.
- Do not insert new top-level sections between the title (`# **Apple**`), `## **Round 2**`, and `### **Practice**`; keep that structure intact.
- When the user says they are “adding content” or “adding code” to the notebook, assume they want it under the existing Practice section unless they specify otherwise (e.g. a new Round).
